                <pb facs="0064" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6590H/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-12T09:00:00+04:00">November 12,
                            1943—9 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 13—8:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>222. Italian Government desires Quaroni its Minister here to join Badoglio’s new
                    Foreign Office and suggests that Anzilotti remain in Charge. British Minister
                    has not yet delivered the message as we both feel that Afghan Government will
                    not consent to Anzilotti’s remaining for the reason stated in the second
                    paragraph of Legation’s telegram 178, September 23, 10 a.m. British Minister is
                    awaiting further instructions from his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
